MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Beatles 1967 1970 feels like a natural next choice after Sgt. Pepper's because I want more songs from that period of the Beatles.",
    "Chronicle, Neil Diamond's greatest hits, and The Best of Bread fit my repeated interest in familiar classic hits, with Bread also matching the softer listening I enjoy from Simon & Garfunkel."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Partners, Title, and It's Time give me too little information to connect them to music I enjoy; passing on them reflects uncertainty rather than a definite dislike.",
    "Adele interests me, but older favorites appeal more today. Likewise, I would choose a Beatles song collection before a live recording."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Liking an artist does not mean I want every recording by them equally; the Beatles connection matters, but the kind of album matters too.",
    "My interest in greatest-hits albums does not mean I want two overlapping Neil Diamond collections in the same listening session."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated choices of best-of collections reflect an interest in familiar songs gathered together, which makes a broad song collection especially appealing right now.",
    "My listening includes newer pop and vocal music, but that does not make those my first choice today; my stronger immediate pull is toward older melodic favorites."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations largely understood my interest in classic hits, but missed how familiarity, album type, and my current mood determine which related albums I would actually choose."
}
